  body: |
    # Country and agreement scope of the cited pension uprating guidance

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source makes its description of Retirement Pension uprating abroad depend on residence, EC personal scope or a relevant agreement, and calls pension not increased by uprating “frozen”.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 075780 and 075783, on a page labelled July 2011, describe a particular historical source regime. No current country list, award rate or new State Pension outcome is inferred.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 075780, PDF page 81](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814b6a40f0b62305b8e2a8/dmgch0705.pdf#page=81)
    - [DMG 075783, PDF page 81](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814b6a40f0b62305b8e2a8/dmgch0705.pdf#page=81)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:20.299037Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication or legal commencement date. The attachment publication date is not established by the frozen metadata. Source-stated dates require their own role and precision.

